  "published": "2026-11-21",
  "updated": "2026-11-21",
  "intro": "Everlance, TripLog, Driversnote, Expensify, Hurdlr, MileageWise and Stride are seven MileIQ alternatives. They differ in free-tier trip limits, in annual versus monthly pricing, and in whether mileage is the whole product or one feature next to expenses, taxes or past-mileage recovery. The table lists each plan's published price, and the sections below turn those prices into yearly totals.\n\n[MileIQ](https://www.mileiq.com/) lists a Free plan at $0 with 40 free drives every month, automatic mileage tracking and auto-generated reports. The Unlimited plan costs $11.66 per month billed annually or $13.99 per month billed monthly, with unlimited drives. MileIQ is published by Bending Spoons, and each drive is classified by swiping left or right before a tax-compliant mileage report is submitted.\n\nFor a wider shortlist, see the [best mileage tracker apps roundup](/roundup/best-mileage-tracker-apps/). The [Internal Revenue Service (IRS) mileage rate for 2026 guide](/mileage-deduction/irs-mileage-rate-2026/) covers the deduction itself. The [standard mileage vs actual expenses guide](/mileage-deduction/standard-mileage-vs-actual-expenses/) compares the two IRS methods, and the [comparison hub](/compare/) holds other software breakdowns.",
  "tableTitle": "MileIQ Alternatives: Published Prices Compared",
  "tableNote": "Prices and plans from each provider's own website, checked November 21, 2026.",
